00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.720
The first question asks, is
it possible to get a cold

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.220
or to get sick from
deliberate cold exposure?

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.580
And I suppose a related
question is, should you even

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.730
do deliberate, cold
exposure if you have

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.302
a sniffle, a cold, or a flu?

00:01:58.302 --> 00:02:00.010
I get that question
all the time as well.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.840
So answer both of
those questions.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.280
And I will also touch on some
of the immune enhancing effects

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.930
of deliberate cold exposure.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.669
But just to make
sure that we answer

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:11.310
the specific question asked
here right off the bat,

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:15.040
is it possible to get a cold
or to get sick from deliberate

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.260
cold exposure?

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.760
Well, assuming that
you're not doing

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.430
the deliberate cold
exposure for more than,

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:24.610
say five or six
minutes at one stretch,

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:28.950
probably not directly from
the deliberate cold exposure.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.390
I mention that
because most people

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.310
are doing anywhere
from about a minute

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.370
to three minutes, sometimes
five or six minutes.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.120
And maybe for those
of you that are really

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.040
pushing it, 10 minutes of
deliberate cold exposure.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.820
And most often after doing
that deliberate cold exposure,

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.620
people are either
getting clothed,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.500
or they're getting into a sauna,
or they're taking a hot shower,

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.050
and then getting clothed and
heading off into their day

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.640
or off to sleep depending
on what time of day or night

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.660
you happen to do your
deliberate cold exposure.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.610
We can safely say
that if you warm up

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:59.280
after a relatively brief,
meaning one minute to,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.985
let's extend out to 10
minutes, 10-minute deliberate

00:03:01.985 --> 00:03:03.360
cold exposure,
although, I really

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.657
want to caution people to
not do 10-minute deliberate

00:03:05.657 --> 00:03:06.990
cold exposure right off the bat.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.240
If you are somebody who
is not accustomed to it,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.800
don't jump right up to that
long exposure to cold water.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.050
Start with shorter exposures.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.400
But if you're doing that
one-to-10-minute deliberate,

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.850
cold exposure, and then
you're getting warm afterwards

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:23.470
and heading about your day, I
can't see how the deliberate

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:27.900
cold exposure itself would
enhance your susceptibility

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.670
to getting sick.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.850
That said, we know
from an enormous number

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.610
of studies that have looked
at cold virus transmission

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.970
and other forms of viral
and bacterial transmission

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.790
that the environment
that you happen to be in

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.940
does impact your
susceptibility to colds

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.300
and other types of viruses
and to bacterial infections

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.170
in the following way.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.500
There have been controlled
studies in which people

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.420
go into laboratories.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.900
Those laboratories have rooms,
which they can very tightly

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.970
control the humidity,
so essentially,

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.340
the water content
in the air, as well

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.050
as the temperature in the room.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:07.360
And if you look at the
total mass of those data,

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.690
we can say a couple
of specific things

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.160
in kind of bullet point fashion.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.880
First off, cold,
dry air does seem

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.070
to increase our
susceptibility to

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.930
viral and bacterial infections.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.810
Because whether or not you're
a mouth breather or a nose

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.300
breather, and by the way, I
suggest everyone be a nose

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.550
breather unless you're
exercising hard enough that you

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.008
have to breathe
through your mouth,

00:04:28.008 --> 00:04:30.010
or you're talking or
something of that sort.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:34.210
But if you're a nose breather
or a mouth breather or both,

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:38.140
viruses and bacteria enter
through your nose and mouth,

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.505
sometimes through your eyes,
but your nose and mouth

00:04:40.505 --> 00:04:42.130
are going to be the
main sites of entry

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.320
and your main barriers to
viral and bacterial infections.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:48.040
In fact, one of the ways you
are constantly fighting off

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.810
bacterial and viral
infections that you're

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.110
exposed to all
the time is by way

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.240
of those viruses
and bacteria getting

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.790
trapped in the mucous
lining of your nose

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:01.310
or your mouth, most notably
in the back of your throat.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:05.140
So if you spend time in
cold, dry environments,

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:08.080
there is a tendency for that
mucosal lining to be thinner.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.450
There is a tendency
for that mucosal lining

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.813
to not be as robust in general.

00:05:12.813 --> 00:05:14.230
And when I say
robust, what I mean

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.240
is that if your mouth
breathing, for instance

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:19.300
in a cold, dry environment,
I'm thinking from the time

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.850
I spent in Cambridge,
Massachusetts in winter

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:23.110
at the T station.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.970
If you're I'm just
imagining myself

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.880
because it was so darn
cold back there breathing

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.010
through your mouth or
having gone for a run,

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:33.520
and your mouth isn't covered,
or even if you're deliberately

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.280
nasal breathing, you are
drying out your nasal passages

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.640
and making them more
susceptible to infections.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.932
Does that necessarily
mean that every time you

00:05:41.932 --> 00:05:43.390
go out in cold,
dry air that you're

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:44.500
going to get an infection?

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.850
No, of course it doesn't.

00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:49.150
But to relate this back to
the question we have before,

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:52.300
there are a lot of data pointing
to the fact that more humid,

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:56.320
warm environments are going
to make your mucosal lining

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.010
and the general upper
respiratory area more,

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.510
I don't want to say
immune because I

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:03.460
don't want to conflate that
word with the other meaning

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:03.960
of immune.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.600
It's going to make it
more robust against

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.040
bacterial and viral infections.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:14.800
So if you get into a cold
shower or a cold plunge

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.920
or a cold ocean or a cold
lake, and then you get out,

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.080
and you're out there
shivering and shaking, trying

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.120
to boost your
metabolism or whatever

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.910
it is that you're
doing it for, and it's

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.490
cold, dry air, and
especially if your mouth

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.800
breathing in that
cold, dry air, yes, I

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:32.110
could see how that
might lead to a higher

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:35.770
probability of getting a cold
or other type of infection.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:38.620
But there's nothing specific
about the deliberate, cold

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:43.150
exposure itself that can
induce a cold or other type

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:45.427
of infection assuming that
the water is clean, right?

00:06:45.427 --> 00:06:47.260
We're not talking about
bacterial infections

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.640
of cuts on the skin, et cetera.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.940
We're talking about colds and
other forms of being sick,

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.430
namely upper
respiratory infections.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:58.810
OK, now with that said, I
often get asked whether or not

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.240
for people who already
have a little sniffle,

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:04.210
they're feeling a little run
down or perhaps a lot run down,

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.800
should they do
deliberate cold exposure?

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:09.880
And what's a little tricky
to give a one size fits all

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.840
answer, , but I think we can
safely say that if you are

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:16.540
feeling malaise, if you're
feeling like you have to rest

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.830
you're tired, you're not
feeling good because of a cold

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.660
or because of a flu or because
of a bacterial infection, now,

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.800
I'm not saying just
feeling not good,

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.760
I'm saying feeling not good
due to a cold or other form

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.820
of virus or bacterial infection,
then I would say stay out

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.050
of deliberate, cold exposure.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:36.247
Don't use it.

00:07:36.247 --> 00:07:37.330
Now, why would I say that?

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:39.622
Given the data I'll talk
about in a few minutes showing

00:07:39.622 --> 00:07:43.220
that regular deliberate cold
exposure if done correctly,

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:46.510
can in fact increase
immune system markers

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:49.670
and perhaps even make you
much more robust to combating

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:51.670
different types of infection
through the release

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:52.480
of adrenaline.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.315
We'll talk about what
all that looks like

00:07:54.315 --> 00:07:55.690
in a moment in
terms of protocols

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:56.690
and some of the science.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:08:00.940
But to just be very clear and
very direct, if you're sick,

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:03.040
stay out of deliberate
cold exposure.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.020
There, I, would
instead recommend

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:09.130
warmer hot baths warmer hot
showers, the sauna, et cetera.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:13.360
But I also would caution that
if you are getting into saunas

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.190
that are too hot,
saunas they're so

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:18.087
hot that it's stressful for
you, and again, a lot of people

00:08:18.087 --> 00:08:20.170
use deliberate heat exposure
because of the stress

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:22.930
it induces, they're
doing some heat induced,

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:25.630
for instance, heat shock
proteins and different ways

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.830
of increasing heart rate.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.600
That's a different
sort of thing.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:33.010
That's hard, stressful in order
to generate an adaptation.

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.809
I don't recommend doing that.

00:08:34.809 --> 00:08:37.412
In fact, I don't recommend
doing deliberate cold exposure,

00:08:37.412 --> 00:08:39.370
exercise, or deliberate
heat exposure if you're

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.770
feeling really not well.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.960
Now, if you're feeling
just a little bit not well,

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.002
you're feeling a little
bit rundown, a little bit

00:08:46.002 --> 00:08:49.030
of sniffle, a little bit
of malaise, well then,

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:50.882
it's kind of an edge
case where we could

00:08:50.882 --> 00:08:52.090
say, all right you know what?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.870
Just take a hot shower
and go to sleep.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.470
That's probably the best advice,
that good old-fashioned advice.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.670
But if you are determined to do
your deliberate cold exposure

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:03.760
anyway, then I would
say definitely get warm

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:07.120
or take a hot shower afterwards,
hot bath, or hot sauna,

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.308
but, not too hot that
it's stressful, of course.

00:09:09.308 --> 00:09:11.350
And keep in mind that one
of the variables that's

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:13.120
been measured quite
a lot in laboratory

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.830
studies of deliberate
cold exposure

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.990
is the increase in
immune system markers.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.320
So I'll provide a few links
to some of these studies.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:23.420
Although, nowadays there
are many, many of them.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:27.160
But it's very clear that
deliberate cold exposure

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:31.570
can increase the release
and the production

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:34.140
of different immune
molecules and immune cells.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:37.680
One slightly older study,
but nonetheless a good study

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.570
that has relevance
here is entitled

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:43.470
"Immune system of cold exposed
and cold adapted humans."

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.350
Keep in mind that this study
is a little bit extreme.

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.090
And there are reasons for that.

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.970
I guess to make a long
story short, oftentimes,

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:54.670
in order to quote unquote
"see an effect in a study,"

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:57.330
scientists will use conditions
that are pretty extreme

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.910
compared to control group.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.660
Oftentimes, you'll see
a dose response to,

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:03.442
but it's a little bit trickier
to do with human studies

00:10:03.442 --> 00:10:04.650
of deliberate, cold exposure.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:06.160
It can be done,
but not too common.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.830
But here, they
used a pretty what

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.300
I would call extreme stimulus.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:12.870
It was exposing people to
14 degrees Celsius water,

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:16.060
so that's 57.2
degrees Fahrenheit,

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.290
which isn't that cold.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:19.920
It's like cool, I would
say very cool water,

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:22.200
but not what you might
consider cold depending

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.520
on how well you tolerate cold.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:24.780
And that will vary, of course.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.930
But they had people exposed
to that for an hour, which

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.370
is a pretty long time.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:32.400
Most people, as I mentioned,
are using colder temperatures

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:35.550
of deliberate cold
exposure, so even high 30s,

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:39.240
low 40s, maybe upper
40s for anywhere

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.950
from one to 10
minutes, depending

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.630
on how conditioned they are.

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:45.720
And again, don't just jump into
10 minutes of deliberate, cold

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:49.740
exposure, please at 35
degrees or 40 degrees

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:52.330
or even 45 degrees if you aren't
familiar with deliberate cold

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:52.830
exposure.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.128
You have to ease into these
sorts of things over time.

00:10:55.128 --> 00:10:56.670
And if you're
interested in protocols

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.480
for deliberate cold exposure,
we have a zero-cost newsletter

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:00.395
at hubermanlab.com.

00:11:00.395 --> 00:11:01.770
Go to the Menu,
go to Newsletter,

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:02.790
and you can find that.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:06.300
We've done several episodes
on deliberate cold exposure.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.960
In any event, this study,
"Immune system of cold exposing

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.860
cold adapted humans,"
as I mentioned,

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.940
had people in 14 degrees
Celsius water for one hour.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.970
And basically what they found
is that one exposure to cold

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.070
did not change immune
system function

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.780
in any kind of significant way.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:25.530
However, what they found
was if people did deliver

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:29.070
cold exposure repeatedly over
a period of about six weeks,

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:32.700
and by repeatedly, I mean three
times per week, what they found

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:33.990
were trends.

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:37.180
And again, trends are not
statistically significant,

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:41.190
but trends towards increases in
plasma concentrations of things

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:45.180
like IL 6, interleukin 6 or
total numbers of T lymphocytes

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.030
and T helper cells
and T suppressor cells

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.770
and activated T
and B lymphocytes,

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.800
these are all immune
cells and immune molecules

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:56.200
that roughly correspond to
an increase in immune system

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:56.700
function.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:58.290
If you'd like to learn more
about the immune system,

00:11:58.290 --> 00:12:00.207
I did an episode on
immune system function.

00:12:00.207 --> 00:12:02.040
Again, you can find
that at hubermanlab.com.

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.870
And it spells out
the basic cell types

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:06.482
of what's called the innate
and the adaptive immune system.

00:12:06.482 --> 00:12:08.940
This study, which we will link
to in the show note captions

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:11.970
is but one study of several
other studies showing

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.310
that deliberate cold exposure
can increase immune system

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.830
markers, especially when
deliberate cold exposure is

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:19.470
done repeatedly over time,
so in this case, three times

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:20.918
a week over a
period of six weeks.

00:12:20.918 --> 00:12:22.710
But again, I want to
highlight these aren't

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:24.010
highly significant effects.

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:25.590
These are trends
in the direction

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:28.480
of increased numbers of immune
cells and immune markers.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.780
Now, what's
impossible to know is

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:34.740
how those trends translate
to actual resistance

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:37.980
to specific concentrations of,
say cold virus or flu virus

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.630
or any other virus or bacteria.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:42.120
That would be great, but
that's a very difficult study

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:44.730
to do, especially in the context
of deliberate cold exposure

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:45.520
as well.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:50.010
Now, we can all be scientists
about this and say, what is it

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.800
about deliberate cold
exposure that would increase

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.120
immune system function?

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:57.150
And there, we can
confidently say the molecules

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.980
epinephrine and
norepinephrine, which

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:02.280
are released in both brain and
body in response to cold water

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:06.930
exposure, as well as things like
deliberate hyperventilation,

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.540
the release of norepinephrine
and epinephrine into the brain

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:12.870
and body is known to have a
number of different effects

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:14.190
related to the immune system.

00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:17.850
It can be pro-immune, at
least in the short term.

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:21.978
And in the long term, meaning
if noradrenaline and adrenaline,

00:13:21.978 --> 00:13:24.270
again those are just different
names for norepinephrine

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:24.960
and epinephrine.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:26.070
I'm sorry, those
are the same thing,

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.080
but that's why I use
them interchangeably so

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.247
that you don't get confused.

00:13:29.247 --> 00:13:31.980
If you see noradrenaline
or norepinephrine,

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.650
that's the same thing you hear,
epinephrine or adrenaline,

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:36.390
same thing.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.760
Deliberate cold exposure or
deliberate hyperventilation

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:43.260
will increase those molecules,
norepinephrine and epinephrine.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.660
And their increase
is pro-immune.

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:50.100
It can trigger the
activation of immune cells

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.840
and immune molecules
that can make

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.790
you more resistant to
certain forms of infection.

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:57.060
However, if norepinephrine
and epinephrine

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:59.610
are elevated chronically,
and especially

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:02.940
if they are elevated late
in the day repeatedly

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:06.330
over many, many days,
that can cause reductions

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:09.390
in the number and
efficiency of immune cells

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:10.780
in combating infections.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.685
So getting cold
in this context of

00:14:12.685 --> 00:14:14.310
whether or not you
can get sick from it

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:15.930
should really be
considered more as

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:19.470
what happens when you spike your
adrenaline and norepinephrine?

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:21.780
And there's one other
study that we can look to,

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:24.510
which is now really a famous
study published in proceedings

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.130
of the National
Academy of Sciences

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.410
looking at so-called
Wim Hof breathing.

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:31.650
But really, that just translates
to cyclic hyperventilation.

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:33.320
So this is inhaling
through nose,

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:36.220
exhaling through the mouth
repeatedly 25 times or so.

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.950
[BREATHING]

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:41.825
If you do that, you notice
you feel quite warm,

00:14:41.825 --> 00:14:43.950
lots to do with some things
relate to vasodilation,

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:46.110
has some things to do with
release of norepinephrine.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.430
And epinephrine, we
know that pattern

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:49.660
of deliberate hyperventilation,
much like deliberate

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:52.590
cold exposure,
deploys or releases

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:55.350
noradrenaline and adrenaline
into your brain and body.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:57.270
And we know from
this study entitled

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.580
"Voluntary activation of the
sympathetic nervous system

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.340
and attenuation of the innate
immune response in humans"

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:04.500
showed really nicely, I think.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:09.720
That if people are injected
with E. coli, a bacteria

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.220
it's actually an
end-- they did this

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:12.600
through endotoxin injections.

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:13.950
People got really sick.

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:16.260
They'd get feel like
they had the flu,

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:19.050
they vomit, diarrhea,
get a fever, et cetera.

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.150
However if they did
the sorts of breathing

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:24.600
that I talked about just a
moment ago, prior to that,

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:29.250
they were able to ward off a
lot of the symptoms associated

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.050
with the endotoxin infection.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:33.660
And you would say, OK wow, their
immune system just fired up,

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:34.920
and they were able
to fight it off.

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:36.570
But it's trickier
than that, actually.

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:39.030
What happened was the
release of epinephrine

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:41.910
and norepinephrine from
cyclic hyperventilation, which

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:44.160
is really what
[BREATHING] really

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.580
is, cyclic hyperventilation,
also called Wim Hof breathing,

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:50.700
also called tummo breathing,
et cetera, that actually had

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:55.620
a suppressive action on certain
arms of the immune system

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:59.010
in a way that allowed
people to avoid symptomology

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:01.950
such as fever,
nausea, et cetera.

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:03.870
And we would imagine
the same thing would

00:16:03.870 --> 00:16:06.570
occur with deliberate
cold exposure done

00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:10.600
prior to bacterial
infection or viral exposure.

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.530
So if you're sensing that I'm
saying two things at once,

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:14.430
I am.

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:16.360
I'm saying deliberate
cold exposure,

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:19.200
and cyclic hyperventilation
can both cause deployment

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:23.460
of molecules such as
epinephrine and norepinephrine

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.930
that lead to enhanced
immune system

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:26.340
function if done repeatedly.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.760
I'm also saying that increasing
norepinephrine and epinephrine

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:33.480
too much can suppress
your immune system.

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:36.415
In this study, the PNAS study
that I mentioned a moment ago,

00:16:36.415 --> 00:16:38.040
that suppression of
the immune response

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:40.740
was actually one of the reasons
people avoided symptomology.

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:42.762
But they were still
injected with endotoxin,

00:16:42.762 --> 00:16:45.220
so they just weren't fighting
off the endotoxin with fever.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:48.360
Remember, fever is an
adaptation to fight infection.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.180
It's designed essentially
to heat up the infection

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.120
and kill it.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:54.570
So what are we to
take away from this?

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.420
Here are what I think
are the key takeaways.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:00.510
One, if you are
feeling good to great,

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:02.350
do your deliberate
cold exposure.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:05.730
And perhaps don't worry so
much about using your body's

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.760
natural metabolism and
thermogenic abilities

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.510
to heat back up afterwards.

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:13.589
But I don't suggest anyone
ever allow themselves

00:17:13.589 --> 00:17:15.819
to stay really cold
after deliberate

00:17:15.819 --> 00:17:19.349
cold exposure for more than
10, 15 minutes or maybe

00:17:19.349 --> 00:17:20.609
half an hour, right?

00:17:20.609 --> 00:17:22.500
Get bundled back up,
or put on clothes.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:25.619
If it's a nice hot, sunny day,
get out in the sun and warm up.

00:17:25.619 --> 00:17:27.210
Again, temperatures
and conditions

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:32.000
will vary for different people,
different locations, et cetera.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.670
If you are not
feeling great, you're

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:35.452
feeling a little
rundown, and you really

00:17:35.452 --> 00:17:37.160
want to do your
deliberate cold exposure,

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.710
do it, but then warm up
really well afterwards.

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:44.040
Maybe even drink some hot tea or
other fluid afterwards as well.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.820
And if you are not feeling
good, you're feeling malaise,

00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:48.650
you're feeling run down.

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:51.810
Despite what you read
about deliberate,

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:54.350
cold exposure or cyclic
hyperventilation,

00:17:54.350 --> 00:17:57.260
allowing for the deployment
of immune molecules

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.000
or increasing the
number of immune cells

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:01.910
that you're making,
avoid anything

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:05.240
that's stressful or
challenging whether or not

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:08.385
it's a cold challenge, a heat
challenge, or an exercise

00:18:08.385 --> 00:18:10.010
challenge when you're
feeling run down.

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:12.427
Because under those conditions,
what you really want to do

00:18:12.427 --> 00:18:14.240
is slow your circulation
down, probably

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:15.948
find and take a little
walks or something

00:18:15.948 --> 00:18:18.290
provided you're not doubled
over in bed and vomiting,

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:18.830
and things like that.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:20.247
A little bit of
movement, probably

00:18:20.247 --> 00:18:21.560
good to circulate your blood.

00:18:21.560 --> 00:18:23.750
But in general,
the advice that you

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:27.080
get to rest when you're
sick and not push yourself,

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.880
that's really good
advice because you

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.590
want all of your
body's resources

00:18:30.590 --> 00:18:33.860
to be devoted to getting
over that infection.

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:36.470
And if you're interested
in sickness and sickness

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.400
behavior and the
sorts of behaviors

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.400
that can combat infection,
check out the episode

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:41.540
I did on the immune system.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.070
We'll link to it in
the show note captions.

00:18:43.070 --> 00:18:44.487
Because it talks
about how when we

00:18:44.487 --> 00:18:46.580
have a viral or
bacterial infection,

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.050
a whole set of
brain circuits get

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:52.190
activated that encourage us to
be more in the fetal position,

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:56.010
to move less, to be eyes
down, to kind of slump down.

00:18:56.010 --> 00:18:57.490
That's not a coincidence.

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.990
That's because of the activation
of these so-called sickness

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.400
circuits that are
really designed

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:02.990
to help you heal yourself.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:07.040
So I both apologize, and
what do the kids say?

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.150
Sorry, not sorry.

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:12.560
Don't apologize for the
somewhat nuanced answer here.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:14.480
Because a lot of
information out there says,

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.632
oh, cold boosts
your immune system.

00:19:16.632 --> 00:19:18.590
And yeah, that's true
under certain conditions.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.990
It can also deplete
your immune system

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:23.270
and limit your ability
to fight off infections

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:24.860
under other conditions.

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:27.260
And perhaps the last
thing to say about this

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:31.725
is that I am a big believer in
using nasal breathing whenever

00:19:31.725 --> 00:19:33.600
you don't have to breathe
through your mouth.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:35.360
So if you're exercising
hard, by all means breathe

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:35.990
through your mouth.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:37.100
If you're doing
martial arts, and it

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:38.975
requires that you breathe
through your mouth,

00:19:38.975 --> 00:19:40.140
go ahead and do that.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:42.620
But if you're doing, say a
zone two cardio, low level

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:44.340
cardio, or you're
just walking along,

00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:46.598
it's very clear based on
a growing amount of data

00:19:46.598 --> 00:19:48.140
that being a nasal
breather is better

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:49.250
than being a mouth breather.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:50.570
And there are a number
of different reasons

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:53.040
for that we've talked about
on the podcast and elsewhere.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:56.780
But one of the additional
reasons is a main site of entry

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:58.800
for infections is
through the mouth.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:02.070
So keep that mouth shut
unless you need to talk.

